import sys; sys.path.insert(0,"/workspace/social/posts"); from build10 import build
B=r'''<style>.box p,.box li{font-size:18.5px;line-height:1.27}.box h2{font-size:24px;margin-bottom:4px}.code{font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.34}.tbl{font-size:16px}.tbl th,.tbl td{padding:3px 6px}.iq ol{font-size:17px;line-height:1.28}.pill{font-size:13.5px}.grid{gap:9px}.handle{bottom:-12px}.box{padding:9px 11px}.tagline{font-size:18px;margin-bottom:7px}.note{font-size:15px}</style>
<div class="title">🧰 HxGN EAM Inventory Kitting <span class="badge">CHEAT SHEET</span></div>
<div class="tagline">Pre-stage parts and assets as a kit, issue it, take it back, break it up — with lot and expiry control. (Infor EAM Inventory Kitting brief)</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="box c1"><h2>1. What &amp; why</h2><ul><li>Pre-stage a collection of <b>parts and assets</b> as one kit</li><li>Load or deploy with minimal delay</li><li>Keeps inventory control + <b>shelf life</b> (expiry) awareness</li><li>For material managers &amp; supply clerks</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c2"><h2>2. Organization Options</h2><table class="tbl"><tr><th>Code</th><th>Controls</th></tr><tr><td><b>KITLDESC</b></td><td>default Kit Lot Description (Build Kit)</td></tr><tr><td><b>KITPPULD</b></td><td>YES = Part Pulled box pre-checked</td></tr><tr><td><b>LOTIEXPL</b></td><td>NO = can&apos;t issue an expired lot</td></tr><tr><td><b>ISSTOEMP</b></td><td>issue to employees: YES / NO / KITS ONLY</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="box c3"><h2>3. Track as Kit — blocked if</h2><ul><li>Part already has <b>transactions</b></li><li>Part is on a Requisition, PO, RFQ or Blanket Order</li><li>Part exists on another <b>Kit Template</b></li><li>Part has a <b>Preferred Supplier</b></li></ul><div class="note">Decide kit parts up front — create them as new part codes.</div></div>
<div class="box c4"><h2>4. What ticking it does</h2><ul><li>Track by Asset, Fugitive Gas, Repairable Spares → cleared + protected</li><li>Track by Lot, Prevent Reorders → set + protected</li><li>Tracking Method = <b>Stock</b></li><li>Preferred Supplier protected</li><li>Untick → fields unprotected again</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c5"><h2>5. Part screen tabs</h2><ul><li><b>Kit Template</b> tab: which parts / assets + quantities make the kit</li><li><b>Stores</b> tab: <b>Default Return Bin</b> for returned parts</li><li><b>Prevent Issue from Default Return Bin</b> (checked by default)</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c6"><h2>6. Build Kit screen</h2><div class="flow" style="flex-wrap:wrap;row-gap:5px"><span class="pill">Header: kit, store, no. of kits, expiry</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Retrieve Parts</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">F9: Bin / Lot / Asset ID</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Build Kit</span></div><ul style="margin-top:5px"><li>Part expiry must be ≥ Kit Lot Expiration Date</li><li>Any Track-by-Asset part → kits to build = 1, one line per asset</li><li>Print Build Kit List = pick list</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c7"><h2>7. Issue to employees</h2><ul><li><b>Issue/Return Parts</b> screen supports employee issues/returns</li><li>Governed by ISSTOEMP + LOTIEXPL</li><li>Employee screen: <b>Transactions</b> and <b>Outstanding Issues</b> tabs (read-only, kit Dataspies)</li><li>Label each physical kit with its <b>Lot Number</b></li></ul></div>
<div class="box c8"><h2>8. Breakup Kit screen</h2><ul><li>Receive a kit back from a WO, asset, employee…</li><li>Header: Kit Part + Kit Lot → <b>Retrieve Parts</b></li><li>Each line: return to store · move to repair bin · mark <b>used</b></li><li>Print Kit Restock List</li><li>Or return intact via bin-to-bin transfer</li></ul></div>
<div class="box c1" style="grid-column:1 / span 2"><h2>9. Restrictions on a kit part</h2><ul><li>No Preferred Supplier (Stores / Suppliers tabs of Part, Parts tab of Supplier)</li><li>No manual stock details (bin, lot, quantity) — stock comes from Build Kit</li><li>Part number can&apos;t switch non-kit ↔ kit</li><li>Can&apos;t be ordered, requisitioned, RFQ&apos;d or blanket ordered; not allowed on a Non-PO Receipt</li></ul></div>
<div class="bottom">
<div class="box" style="border-color:#1a5f7a"><h2 style="color:#1a5f7a">10a. Kit lifecycle</h2><div class="flow"><span class="pill">Org Options</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Track as Kit + Template</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Build Kit</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Issue</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Breakup Kit</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="pill">Restock / repair / used</span></div></div>
<div class="box iq"><h2>10b. Consultant tips</h2><ol><li>Set LOTIEXPL = NO for shelf-life parts</li><li>Use KITS ONLY if only kits go to staff</li><li>Agree a lot-label procedure</li><li>Review Outstanding Issues regularly</li></ol></div>
<div class="box" style="border-color:#2d8a5a"><h2 style="color:#2d8a5a">10c. Key points</h2><ul><li>Kit = lot-tracked</li><li>Never purchased</li><li>Built from stock</li></ul></div>
</div></div>'''
build("/workspace/social/posts/2026-10-16-linkedin-eam-inventory-kitting",B,1350,"Rahul Kumar")
